c xlink:href="jksc-27-194-g002"/></fig><fig id="F3" position="float"><label>Fig. 3</label><caption><p>Compared figure with excepted vs. included coagulation zone.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jksc-27-194-g003"/></fig><table-wrap id="T1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Characteristics of the patients</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jksc-27-194-i001"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>Values are presented as number (%).</p><p>Comorbidity is disease of two or more organs, such as the heart, lung, kidney or endocrine organ.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T2" position="float"><label>Table 2</label><caption><p>Clinicopathologic characteristics of polyps</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jksc-27-194-i002"/><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>Values are presented as number (%).</p><p><sup>a</sup>&#x02265;2 mm. <sup>b</sup>1 mm &#x02264; but &#x0003c; 2 mm. <sup>c</sup>&#x0003c;1 mm.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T3" position="float"><label>Table 3</label><caption><p>Characteristics of resection margin on the review slide</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="jksc-27-194-i003"/></table-wrap></floats-group></article>